§ CSLv3 TYPE SYSTEM
I> elevated to own file — was scattered across v2 sources
I> reconciled: specs/ (practical primitives, determinatives), pasted (dependent, linear, algebraic)
I> layered: primitives → compound → algebraic → dependent → linear

§ PRIMITIVE TYPES
  | type  | bits | semantics                    |
  |-------|------|------------------------------|
  | u8    | 8    | unsigned byte                |
  | u16   | 16   | unsigned short               |
  | u32   | 32   | unsigned int                 |
  | u64   | 64   | unsigned long                |
  | i8    | 8    | signed byte                  |
  | i16   | 16   | signed short                 |
  | i32   | 32   | signed int                   |
  | i64   | 64   | signed long                  |
  | f32   | 32   | IEEE 754 float               |
  | f64   | 64   | IEEE 754 double              |
  | bool  | 1    | true | false                 |
  | str   | var  | UTF-8 string                 |

§ SPATIAL TYPES (LoA domain)
  | type  | layout          | semantics              |
  |-------|-----------------|------------------------|
  | vec2  | [f32;2]         | 2D vector              |
  | vec3  | [f32;3]         | 3D vector              |
  | vec4  | [f32;4]         | 4D vector / RGBA       |
  | mat4  | [f32;4,4]       | 4×4 matrix             |
  | quat  | [f32;4]         | unit quaternion         |
  | rgba  | [f32;4]         | color (0..1 per channel)|

§ COMPOUND TYPES
  [T;N]         → fixed-length array of T, size N
  [T;_]         → dynamic array / slice
  T | U         → union / either / sum
  T?            → optional (T | nil)
  T!            → result (T | error)
  (T, U, V)     → tuple (product, positional)
  {K: V}        → map / associative
  &T            → reference / borrow (shared)
  *T            → collection / repeated

§ ALGEBRAIC TYPES (from pasted v2 §07)
  sum:     T₁ | T₂ | ...                   # tagged union
  product: ⟨f₁: T₁, f₂: T₂, ...⟩          # struct / record
  
  def DamageType't = enum[
    physical { slash, pierce, blunt }
    elemental { fire, ice, lightning, earth, water, wind }
    arcane { void, radiant, necrotic }
  ]

§ DEPENDENT TYPES (from pasted v2 §07, Agda lineage)
  Π⟨x: T⟩ → U(x)        # pi-type (dependent function / for-all)
  Σ⟨x: T, y: U(x)⟩      # sigma-type (dependent pair / exists)
  
  ex:
    Π⟨n: ɴ⟩ → ᴠ⟨f32; n⟩   # fn returning vector whose length depends on input
    Σ⟨n: ɴ, v: ᴠ⟨f32; n⟩⟩ # pair of length + vector of that length

§ REFINEMENT TYPES
  { x: T ⊢ P(x) }       # subset type: all x:T satisfying P
  
  ex:
    { x: f32 ⊢ x > 0 }            # positive floats
    { hp: u16 ⊢ hp ≤ max_hp }     # bounded health
    { v: vec3 ⊢ |v| ≈ 1.0 }       # unit vectors

§ LINEAR / AFFINE TYPES (from pasted v2 §07)
  T!lin         → must-use-exactly-once (linear)
  T&            → borrowed reference (shared, read-only)
  T&mut         → borrowed reference (exclusive, read-write)
  
  I> critical for: GPU buffer ownership, resource lifecycle
  I> prevents: use-after-free, double-free, leaked resources

§ TYPE CLASS MARKERS (unicode, optional — see §01 tier-1)
  ɴ             → numeric class (any numeric type)
  ꜱ             → string/symbol class
  ʙ             → bool class
  ᴠ             → vector/array class
  ᴍ             → map/associative class
  ʈ             → trait/interface marker
  
  ex:
    fn sum ⟨a: ᴠ⟨ɴ⟩⟩ → ɴ           # sum any numeric vector
    ᴠ⟨ɴ32⟩ = [ɴ32;_]               # vector of 32-bit numerics

§ DETERMINATIVE SUFFIXES (ASCII fallback — see §01 tier-1)
  hp'd          → hp is a data value
  render'f      → render is a function
  physics's     → physics is a system
  Material't    → Material is a type
  player'e      → player is an entity
  iron'm        → iron is a material
  density'p     → density is a property
  alive'g       → alive is a gate/bool
  max_hp'r      → max_hp is a rule/constraint
  
  W! use when context ¬ disambiguates
  R! omit when context makes category obvious (default=silent)

§ TYPE INFERENCE RULES
  bare number  → f32 (float default) or i32 (integer default)
  bare string  → str
  bare bool    → bool
  undecorated noun @ top indent → module/system
  undecorated noun @ property position → data field
  undecorated verb → function/operation
  colon w/o RHS → scope introduction (block follows)

§ RANK POLYMORPHISM (APL lineage, from pasted §07)
  scalar op: fn f (x: T) → T
  elevated:  fn f (x: ᴠ⟨T⟩) → ᴠ⟨T⟩     # auto-lifted
  rank-k:    fn f (x: ᴠᵏ⟨T⟩) → ᴠᵏ⟨T⟩   # k-dimensional lift
  R! ops broadcast like numpy
  W! explicit rank annotation when ambiguous
∎
